 Groups not listed in `group_rules` fall back to `default_group_policy` (defaults to the value of `FEISHU_GROUP_POLICY`).
 
+## Group History Backfill
+
+Hermes can fetch recent Feishu group messages and prepend them to the current
+agent turn as `channel_context`. This lets the bot answer ordinary group
+follow-ups with recent room context without permanently importing the whole
+group transcript into Hermes conversation history.
+
+The Feishu API used is `GET /open-apis/im/v1/messages` with
+`container_id_type=chat`. Feishu requires the bot to be in the queried group.
+For app/tenant-token access to group history, the app must have a message-read
+scope plus `im:message.group_msg`.
+
+```yaml
+feishu:
+  history_backfill: true
+  history_backfill_limit: 20
+  history_backfill_seconds: 1800
+  history_backfill_max_chars: 6000
+  attachment_backfill_window_seconds: 300
+  attachment_backfill_max_messages: 3
+  attachment_backfill_max_files: 6
+  attachment_backfill_timeout_seconds: 8
+  assistant_identity_throttle_messages: 20
+  assistant_identity_throttle_seconds: 600
+```
+
+| Setting | Default | Description |
+|---------|---------|-------------|
+| `history_backfill` | `false` | Fetch recent group messages for the current turn |
+| `history_backfill_limit` | `20` | Maximum historical messages to include |
+| `history_backfill_seconds` | `1800` | Time window before the trigger message |
+| `history_backfill_max_chars` | `6000` | Maximum formatted context characters |
+| `attachment_backfill_window_seconds` | `300` | Same-sender window for a standalone image/file/video/audio followed by @Hermes |
+| `attachment_backfill_max_messages` | `3` | Maximum recent attachment messages recovered for one trigger |
+| `attachment_backfill_max_files` | `6` | Maximum files recovered for one trigger, including quoted attachments |
+| `attachment_backfill_timeout_seconds` | `8` | Attachment recovery deadline before a visible failure status is injected |
+| `assistant_identity_throttle_messages` | `20` | Suppress repeated assistant self-introductions if one appears in this many recent group messages |
+| `assistant_identity_throttle_seconds` | `600` | Suppress repeated assistant self-introductions if one appears in this many seconds |
+
+History backfill is skipped for Feishu DMs. Deleted messages, the trigger
+message, and Hermes' own prior bot messages are excluded from the context block.
+Merged forwarded messages (`merge_forward`) are expanded through the message
+detail API when possible; nested images and files are recovered as normal
+inbound attachments. Reply/history text contains only path-free placeholders;
+the resource bytes travel through the attachment pipeline exactly once.
+
+## Missed Event Backfill
+
+`history_backfill` only adds context after Hermes has already received a trigger
+message. If the WebSocket connection was stale or offline when someone mentioned
+the bot, Hermes may not receive that trigger event until much later. Missed event
+backfill handles this transport recovery case separately: after startup, gateway
+reconnect, or the Lark SDK's internal WebSocket reconnect, Hermes scans recent
+messages in known chats and replays only unseen messages that pass the normal
+Feishu admission rules.
+
+The scan is bounded and does not enumerate the tenant. Target chats come from
+`missed_event_backfill_chats`, the Feishu home channel, explicit `group_rules`
+entries, and `~/.hermes/groups.yaml`. A wildcard `group_rules: "*"` authorizes
+normal inbound admission but is not used as a discovery source.
+
+Replayed messages admit exactly like live events. Each target chat's mode is
+resolved from chat metadata (`chat_mode`): DM targets — including a p2p home
+channel — replay without the group mention gate, while group targets still
+require a mention. If the metadata lookup fails, the chat is treated as a
+group so recovery can never widen admission. A message the user already
+re-asked via quote-reply (with or without a mention) is marked covered when
+that reply is answered, so the recovery scan does not answer it twice.
+
+```yaml
+feishu:
+  missed_event_backfill: true
+  missed_event_backfill_seconds: 21600
+  missed_event_backfill_limit: 50
+  missed_event_backfill_chats:
+    - oc_group_chat_id
+```
+
+| Setting | Default | Description |
+|---------|---------|-------------|
+| `missed_event_backfill` | `true` | Scan known Feishu chats after startup/reconnect for missed trigger messages |
+| `missed_event_backfill_seconds` | `21600` | Time window to scan before the recovery point |
+| `missed_event_backfill_limit` | `50` | Maximum listed messages per target chat |
+| `missed_event_backfill_chats` | `[]` | Extra chat IDs to scan in addition to home channel, explicit rules, and `groups.yaml` |
+
+The replay path uses the same message-id dedup cache as live events. When a user
+manually quotes an earlier missed message and mentions Hermes, the quoted
+message ID is marked covered after that turn is dispatched, so a later delayed
+push or reconnect scan does not answer the same original message again.
+
